gui.packet.captured_id.tip.rule_name.title=§e rule name (name)
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.rule_name.desc=Unique key for use with placeholders, such as {id}. It is recommended to use only letters/numbers/underscores.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.display_name.title=§eDisplayName (displayName)
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.display_name.desc=Only for interface display, Chinese is available. If empty, the rule name is displayed.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.note.title=§eRemarks (note)
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.note.desc=Used for recording purposes, packet capture sources, and precautions. It is recommended to fill it out to facilitate subsequent maintenance.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.aliases.title=§e aliases
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.aliases.desc1=Comma-separated synonymous keys, such as session_id,sessionid.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.aliases.desc2=After filling in, you can use {session_id} or {sessionid} to access the same rule value.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.enabled.title=§e enabled (enabled)
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.enabled.desc=true=enable crawling; false=disable. You can click the button on the right to switch.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.channel.title=§e channel (channel)
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.channel.desc=Only match the network channel name. Empty means no channel restriction.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.direction.title=§e direction (direction)
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.direction.desc=inbound=receive packets, outbound=send packets, both=two-way.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.target.title=§e matches target (target)
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.target.desc=hex=matches on hexadecimal text; decoded=matches on decoded text.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.pattern.title=§eregular expression (pattern)
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.pattern.desc=Must contain a capturing group, such as (...), to extract values from the group specified by group.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.offset.title=§e offset (offset)
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.offset.desc1=Optional, only effective for hex values; examples: -1E, 1E, +1E.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.offset.desc2=Based on the matching value, addition and subtraction offsets will be made in hexadecimal. Leave blank to indicate no offset.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.group.title=§e group
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.group.desc=The capture group number to extract, usually 1.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.value_type.title=§e value type (valueType)
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.value_type.desc=hex=analyze directly in hexadecimal bytes; decimal-int=convert decimal integer to bytes.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.byte_length.title=§ebyte length (byteLength)
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.byte_length.desc=Only decimal-int is commonly used, indicating how many bytes it should be converted into, and the default is 4.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.update_sequence.title=§e Execute sequence when updating
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.update_sequence.desc=Automatically executes the selected path sequence when the capture value of this rule changes. Leave blank to not execute.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.update_sequence_mode.title=§e trigger mode
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.update_sequence_mode.desc=always=executed for every update; first=executed once for the first update; cooldown=executed at the cooling interval; recapture=executed every time a package is rematched.
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.update_sequence_cooldown.title=§eCooling(ms)
gui.packet.captured_id.tip.update_sequence_cooldown.desc=It only takes effect when the trigger mode is cooldown, indicating the minimum interval between two executions.
